===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|en|enm|fight}}, {{m|enm|feyght}}, {{m|enm|fiȝt}}, {{m|enm|fecht}}, from {{inh|en|ang|feoht}}, {{m|ang|ġefeoht}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*fehtan}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*fehtą}}, {{m|gem-pro|*gafehtą|t=fight, struggle}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*fehtaną|t=to struggle with}}. Cognate with {{cog|nl|gevecht}}, {{cog|de|Gefecht}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun|~}}

# An [[occasion]] of fighting.
#: {{ux|en|One of them got stuck in a chokehold and got stabbed to death during the '''fight'''.}}
# {{lb|en|archaic}} A [[battle]] between opposing armies.
# A [[physical]] [[confrontation]] or [[combat]] between two or more people or groups.
#: {{ux|en|Watch your language! Are you looking for a '''fight'''?}}
# {{lb|en|sports}} A [[boxing]] or [[martial arts]] [[match]].
#: {{ux|en|I'm going to Nick’s to watch the big '''fight''' tomorrow night.}}
# A [[conflict]], possibly nonphysical, with opposing ideas or forces; [[strife]].
#: {{ux|en|I'll put up a '''fight''' to save this company.}}
#* {{RQ:Allingham China Governess|chapter=18|passage=‘Then the father has a great '''fight''' with his terrible conscience,’ said Munday with granite seriousness. ‘Should he make a row with the police {{...}}? Or should he say nothing about it and condone brutality for fear of appearing in the newspapers?}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2013-08-10|volume=408|issue=8848|magazine=w:The Economist
|title=[http://www.economist.com/news/leaders/21583270-new-zealands-plan-regulate-designer-drugs-better-trying-ban-them-and-failing-new A new prescription]
|passage=As the world's drug habit shows, governments are failing in their quest to monitor every London window-box and Andean hillside for banned plants. But even that Sisyphean task looks easy next to the '''fight''' against synthetic drugs.}}
# {{lb|en|uncountable}} The [[will]] or [[ability]] to fight.
#: {{ux|en|That little guy has a bit of '''fight''' in him after all.&nbsp;&nbsp; As soon as he saw the size of his opponent, all the '''fight''' went out of him.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} A screen for the combatants in ships; an [[arming]].
#* {{RQ:Dryden Amboyna|page=31|passage=Who ever ſaw a noble ſight, / That never view'd a brave Sea Fight: / Hang up your bloody Colours in the Aire, / Up with your '''Fights''', and your Nettings prepare, / Your Merry Mates chear, with a luſty bold ſpright, / Now each Man his brindice, and then to the '''Fight''', {{...}}}}

